repository-code: 'https://github.com/embodied-computation-group/Cardioception'
url: 'https://www.the-ecg.org/Cardioception/'
abstract: >-
  Cardioception is an open-source Python toolbox for studying how people
  perceive their own heartbeat. Built on PsychoPy, it brings the most widely
  used methods for measuring cardiac interoception together under one
  installation and one output layout: the Heart Rate Discrimination task, the
  Heartbeat Counting task, the Phase Adjustment Task and the Heartbeat
  Synchrony Discrimination task. The pulse is recorded from a USB pulse
  oximeter, or from ECG and PPG devices over Lab Streaming Layer.
keywords:
  - interoception
  - heart rate discrimination
  - heartbeat counting
  - psychophysics
  - metacognition
  - cardiac
  - psychopy
  - heartbeat synchrony
  - phase adjustment task
  - lab streaming layer
